      "problem": "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+8y=-28 \\\\ 2x+3y=11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+8y=-28 \\\\ 2x+3y=11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\,-28 & 8 \\\\ \\,\\,11 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}.\n$$",
